  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoRobins/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoRobins": "HydeCo. Robins!",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoRobins/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoRobins_PrepareToRemove": "Prepare to Remove Mod",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoRobins/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoRobins_PrepareToRemove_tooltip": "Removing this mod from a game where a robin was out at the last save loses the other animals saved around it, your own included. In single player, save once with this version (sleep, or quit), after letting go of any you carry and it should be safe to remove. On a server, turn this on first: no robins come out and any that are out go home; let the server save, then remove the mod.",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoRobins/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoRobins_Robins": "Robins",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoRobins/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoRobins_RobinsNearPlayer": "Most robins out at once",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoRobins/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoRobins_RobinsNearPlayer_tooltip": "How many robins can be out around each player at the same time (6 by default). Lower it to see fewer, raise it for more. 0 stops new robins coming out.",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoRobins/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Sandbox.json|Sandbox_HydeCoRobins_Robins_tooltip": "American robins live in nest trees and hop and peck on the grass nearby. In daylight there are always two robins near nest trees, more from March to October and fewer in the rain. Nest trees drop robin feathers, and sometimes a bird's nest or robin eggs. A robin that sees you flies into a nest tree. Sneaking lets you get closer. A stick trap catches robins alive, and a dead robin gives small-bird meat and feathers.",
  "translate_en|mods/HydeCoRobins/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/Tooltip.json|Tooltip_HydeCoRobins_RobinFeather": "A hundred feathers stuff a pillow or a teddy bear. One feather dipped in black, grey, red, blue or green dye makes a quill that writes in that colour."
